From 60635cdf5aa4db4a32d94289860de0f481a52379 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:29:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: Mark the M clusters' state 16
 as boost

State 16 (4380 MHz) of the M clusters runs at the voltage of states 14
and 15, and a J714s M cluster asked for it settled in state 15 (status
register), so a cluster cannot be relied on to run there. Mark it
turbo-mode: it is then offered with boost on, and the scheduler's
capacity is no longer scaled to a frequency the cluster may decline.

The P cluster's states 18-21 (4332-4608 MHz) are left as they are until
it is known whether the cluster runs them.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-base.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-base.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-base.dtsi
index 1be5e14cb12f..6ee171b9a390 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-base.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-base.dtsi
@@ -159,9 +159,11 @@ opp15 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <4308000000>;
 			opp-level = <15>;
 		};
+		/* Boost: a J714s M cluster asked for it settled in state 15 */
 		opp16 {
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <4380000000>;
 			opp-level = <16>;
+			turbo-mode;
 		};
 	};
 
